{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3kxrAtE9ZWrWtPzKef","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013AgUX1vx6EFgU7Pt31DHe9","name":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-6KXNk7 && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\nold=s[s.index(\"def build_system\"):s.index(\"# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\")]\nnew='''def build_system(a, today):\n    # Two cached segments: static instructions (byte-stable) and the per-athlete tail.\n    # A save_fact only changes the tail, so the instructions stay a cache hit.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n\n'''\nopen('bot.py','w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Fix: save_fact no longer evicts the static instructions from the cache\n\n## Cause\n`build_system` (bot.py) joined `INSTRUCTIONS` and `athlete_context` (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language) into one text block with a single `cache_control` marker. `save_fact` changes the facts, so the prefix hash changed and the next call re-created the whole ~1000-token prompt. This matches `logs/usage.jsonl`: after each `save_fact`, `cache_read_input_tokens` is 0 and `cache_creation_input_tokens` is about 1000.\n\n## Change\n`build_system` now returns two text blocks, each with `cache_control: ephemeral`:\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS` alone. It has no interpolated values, so it is byte-stable across users and days.\n2. `athlete_context(...)`, the volatile per-athlete tail.\n\nA memory write now invalidates only the tail. Nothing else in the code changed. I didn't run the bot or call the API, so this is unverified.\n\n## What I took from the colleague's note\n- **Used:** the two-marker split, and keeping the instructions byte-stable.\n- **Used:** keeping all facts in the tail rather than selecting top-N per message. The code already does that, and I left it.\n- **Used:** leaving the keyword-based tool filtering alone. Tools sit above the system prompt in the cached prefix, but NOTES.md already says to leave the filtering, and the default core tools cover most messages.\n- **Skipped:** the numbers (~780/~240 tokens). They are from the colleague's bot, not this one.\n\n## How to verify\nAgainst the real API, send two messages within 5 minutes. The second should show `cache_read` covering the whole prompt. Then trigger a `save_fact` and send a third message. `cache_read` should still cover the instructions, and `cache_creation` should be only the size of the tail. If `cache_creation` is the size of the whole prompt, something in the instructions is not stable.\nE\npython3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('bot.py').read())\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3086,"cache_read_input_tokens":23352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3086},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5c5bee1-e522-447d-a9ac-3df5e90bdfa8","uuid":"3bc85c43-a7ea-431b-a372-2118202e2c42","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:41:01.854Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3kxdXKZp4e9HdpGukL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013AgUX1vx6EFgU7Pt31DHe9":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-6KXNk7 && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\nold=s[s.index(\"def build_system\"):s.index(\"# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\")]\nnew='''def build_system(a, today):\n    # Two cached segments: static instructions (byte-stable) and the per-athlete tail.\n    # A save_fact only changes the tail, so the instructions 